        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Is the Horizon T202 a good treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              For walking and occasional jogging, yes, on its published figures and two independent reviews. It has a 20 by 60-inch deck, 0.5 to 12 mph, 12 incline levels, a 325 lb rating and lifetime frame and motor cover. Its weaker points are one year of parts cover and a 1.4 mm belt. We have not tested it.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What motor does the Horizon T202 have?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Horizon describes a Johnson Drive System motor but publishes no horsepower rating. Independent reviews give 2.75 HP or 2.75 CHP, which we cannot trace to Horizon. The motor is covered by a lifetime warranty.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How much does the Horizon T202 cost?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On 5 November 2026 Horizon listed it at $899 against a $1,299 reference price, expected to ship the week of 16 November. In mid-October it was $799 with a promotional code. Prices change with promotions, so compare against the best recent price rather than the reference price.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the difference between the Horizon T101 and T202?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The T202 has a 60-inch deck instead of 55 inches, reaches 12 mph instead of 10, has 12 incline levels instead of 10, a 325 lb rating instead of 300 lb, and a 5-inch LCD. The T101 Connect is $200 cheaper and includes JRNY adaptive workouts. Both carry lifetime frame and motor and one-year parts and labour cover.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can you run on a Horizon T202?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              You can jog and run on it; it reaches 12 mph on a 60-inch deck. Independent reviewers recommend it for walkers and occasional joggers and point regular runners to the Horizon 7.0 AT, which has three years of parts cover instead of one.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does the Horizon T202 fold?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Yes. It folds with hydraulic assist from 76 inches long to 48 inches long and 62 inches tall, and it weighs 187 lb.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

